hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27618","Haddathana Waki', he said: Haddathana Sufyan, from Mansur, from Rib'i, from his wife, from a sister of Hudhayfah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressed us and said: O assembly of women, do not adorn yourselves with gold; is there not in silver that with which you may adorn yourselves? No woman among you adorns herself with gold and displays it except that she will be punished with it."
"27619","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Ja'far: Haddathana Shu'bah, from Husayn, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Hudhayfah, from his aunt Fatimah, that she said: We came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, visiting him when sick, among women, and there was a waterskin hung near him with its water dripping upon him from the severity of the heat of the fever. We said: O Messenger of Allah, if you supplicated Allah He would heal you. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Among the severest of people in trial are the prophets, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then those who follow them."
